  (@custom "contractspecv0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\01:Pull `asset`, convert ALL of it into `target` in at most ONE swap, and\0arecord the measured proceeds as a pending per-vault deposit plan. Deposits\0anothing. Auth: owner.\0a\0aThe overflow path for deposits too large to fit one transaction: the user's\0acost is a single signature regardless of how many vaults they picked.\00\00\00\00\00\04fund\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05asset\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05total\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04swap\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09MaybeSwap\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06target\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04plan\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cIntentWeight\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08deadline\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\01SThe NEXT step-wise rebalance op nonce.\0a\0aRead by anything that assembles a rebalance op \e2\80\94 the relay's manual flow and\0athe keeper's executor both need the LIVE value, not a mirrored one. Without\0athis view they would have to trust the indexer's `strategies.nonce`, and a\0amirror that lags by one op makes every subsequent op fail `BadNonce`.\00\00\00\00\05nonce\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05owner\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00:Pause invest/rebalance (withdraw stays open). Auth: admin.\00\00\00\00\00\05pause\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00&The pending deposit intent, or `None`.\00\00\00\00\00\06intent\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06Intent\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\aePull `asset`, deposit across `allocations` by weight, record positions \e2\80\94\0aatomically. Auth: owner.\0a\0a`swaps` maps each vault UNDERLYING that differs from `asset` to the single\0aswap leg used to reach it: **one router call per distinct underlying, not\0aper allocation**. That is a hard budget constraint, not a preference \e2\80\94 the\0afourth router call in a transaction exceeds the memory limit regardless of\0aleg count (see `invest.rs`).\00\00\00\00\00\06invest\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05asset\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05total\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ballocations\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aAllocation\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05swaps\00\00\00\00\00\03\ec\00\00\00\13\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07SwapLeg\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\81Emergency: pull a vault's funds to the **Owner** if its protocol bricks\0a`redeem`. Auth: admin. No fee; callable even when Paused.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06rescue\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05vault\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1cLift the pause. Auth: admin.\00\00\00\07unpause\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00AReplace the contract Wasm. Auth: admin (checked BEFORE the swap).\00\00\00\00\00\00\07upgrade\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dnew_wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\014Withdraw `amount` (underlying; `i128::MAX` = whole position) from one vault\0aback to the owner. Auth: owner. Allowed even when Paused. Both `WithdrawOut`\0avariants are handled live (see `withdraw.rs::deliver`); a cross-asset\0a`Normalize` reverts `AdapterError` while the Router is unset (dormant), not\0aby shape.\00\00\00\08withdraw\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05vault\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06amount\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03out\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bWithdrawOut\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09is_paused\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00nLedger state + raw `shares_held` per open vault. Display value is computed\0aoff-chain (no on-chain value read).\00\00\00\